WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.787
(energetic instrumental music)

00:00:03.787 --> 00:00:06.059
- [Narrator] With seven
billion people on Earth,

00:00:06.059 --> 00:00:08.903
it's a wonder that there are
still corners of this planet

00:00:08.903 --> 00:00:10.736
that remain untouched,

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.558
but one man has made it his
life's work to see them,

00:00:14.558 --> 00:00:17.888
no matter what danger
the journey may bring.

00:00:17.888 --> 00:00:19.437
Mike Libecki has never been one

00:00:19.437 --> 00:00:21.854
to shy away from a challenge.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.433
The former National Geographic
Explorer of the Year

00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:30.680
has completed major expeditions
on all seven continents.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.218
(yelling)

00:00:32.218 --> 00:00:35.277
He's a modern day explorer
who puts his life on the line

00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:36.475
to challenge the idea

00:00:36.475 --> 00:00:39.725
of what humans are capable of enduring.

00:00:41.104 --> 00:00:42.702
His goal: to seek out

00:00:42.702 --> 00:00:46.035
the Earth's last truly untouched places.

00:00:50.441 --> 00:00:52.133
(energetic instrumental music)

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:54.199
- I grew up in California about 30 miles

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:56.071
from Yosemite National Park,

00:00:56.071 --> 00:00:58.335
the center of the universe for climbing.

00:00:58.335 --> 00:01:00.750
My friend's older
brother's friend happened

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.453
to take us out rock climbing one day.

00:01:02.453 --> 00:01:05.687
Totally random, I didn't even
know what rock climbing was,

00:01:05.687 --> 00:01:08.354
and it changed my life that day.

00:01:10.041 --> 00:01:11.678
As soon as I came home from
my first day of climbing

00:01:11.678 --> 00:01:14.746
I was buying a climbing rope,
climbing shoes, harness.

00:01:14.746 --> 00:01:17.184
Climb, climb, climb, that's
all I could think about,

00:01:17.184 --> 00:01:20.951
and that basically evolved
into living in Yosemite,

00:01:20.951 --> 00:01:22.718
climbing El Capitan and Half Dome,

00:01:22.718 --> 00:01:25.149
and to think, oh my gosh,
I could take this climbing

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:26.962
all over the world.

00:01:26.962 --> 00:01:28.536
(playful instrumental music)

00:01:28.536 --> 00:01:30.980
- [Narrator] Libecki's passion
for adventure has taken him

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.322
around the planet to nearly 100 countries,

00:01:34.322 --> 00:01:37.790
but he's not content with
following traditional routes.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.408
His specialty is bagging first ascents.

00:01:41.408 --> 00:01:43.841
- [Mike] First ascent is
basically climbing a route

00:01:43.841 --> 00:01:47.013
or going to the top of a
mountain no one's climbed before,

00:01:47.013 --> 00:01:49.391
so truly going to parts of the planet

00:01:49.391 --> 00:01:51.521
that no human has been to before.

00:01:51.521 --> 00:01:55.604
It really takes every
single thing that you have.

00:01:57.166 --> 00:01:59.001
I mean, these aren't just first ascents.

00:01:59.001 --> 00:02:01.795
These are the most remote,
most demanding first ascents

00:02:01.795 --> 00:02:03.095
and climbs on the planet.

00:02:03.095 --> 00:02:04.474
There is no rescue possibility.

00:02:04.474 --> 00:02:07.104
We're 100% self reliant.

00:02:07.104 --> 00:02:09.401
And I'm not seeking danger or death,

00:02:09.401 --> 00:02:12.646
I'm seeking the ultimate
challenge and the ultimate mystery

00:02:12.646 --> 00:02:14.313
of what's out there.

00:02:15.603 --> 00:02:18.282
- [Narrator] From the
blistering heat of Afghanistan.

00:02:18.282 --> 00:02:20.085
- Sure got hot quick.

00:02:20.085 --> 00:02:22.061
- [Narrator] To the
extreme cold of Canada.

00:02:22.061 --> 00:02:23.670
- [Mike] The weather is getting worse

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.597
and it is cold up here.

00:02:25.597 --> 00:02:27.702
- [Narrator] The climber
turned explorer's trips

00:02:27.702 --> 00:02:30.482
have taken him through every climate.

00:02:30.482 --> 00:02:34.815
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:02:34.815 --> 00:02:36.246
- [Mike] I have thousands
of maps downstairs

00:02:36.246 --> 00:02:40.483
and it's just constant
planning and constant research.

00:02:40.483 --> 00:02:43.441
There's an incredible
amount of physical demand

00:02:43.441 --> 00:02:46.395
of carrying 100 pound loads for 80 miles,

00:02:46.395 --> 00:02:48.825
climbing these big walls,

00:02:48.825 --> 00:02:51.673
enduring all the weather
and the environments.

00:02:51.673 --> 00:02:53.272
Looks like a storm is upon us.

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:56.285
We're a little bit
delirious, cold, dehydrated.

00:02:56.285 --> 00:02:58.212
One of the things I have to do is train.

00:02:58.212 --> 00:03:01.134
I have to be physically
fit to have this lifestyle

00:03:01.134 --> 00:03:05.218
and one of my favorite ways
is to train with my dogs.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:09.298
I have a mother and daughter
dog, Scree and Glacier,

00:03:09.298 --> 00:03:11.420
and they're my favorite training partners,

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.629
and we get out in the mountains,

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:16.046
literally every single day that I'm home.

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:21.516
You really have to work hard
or you will suffer out there.

00:03:23.088 --> 00:03:25.425
Being an explorer has a
lot of responsibilities.

00:03:25.425 --> 00:03:27.811
It's not just going out
and climbing, exploring,

00:03:27.811 --> 00:03:30.621
it's getting people excited
to care more about the planet

00:03:30.621 --> 00:03:32.254
and being able to share these stories

00:03:32.254 --> 00:03:36.289
about the remote places
or these remote cultures.

00:03:36.289 --> 00:03:38.477
- [Narrator] With 23
more trips in the works,

00:03:38.477 --> 00:03:40.245
Libecki is likely to reach his goal

00:03:40.245 --> 00:03:43.115
of 100 expeditions before long.

00:03:43.115 --> 00:03:45.143
- I'm self-diagnosed with OECD

00:03:45.143 --> 00:03:48.419
and that's obsessive
expedition climbing disorder.

00:03:48.419 --> 00:03:50.201
It's my fuel of life.

00:03:50.201 --> 00:03:52.867
I've often thought about
when will I stop going

00:03:52.867 --> 00:03:54.465
on these expeditions and it's basically

00:03:54.465 --> 00:03:56.519
when will the passion stop.

00:03:56.519 --> 00:03:59.728
I hope it never does
because this is a passion,

00:03:59.728 --> 00:04:01.041
this is what I love.

00:04:01.041 --> 00:04:02.624
This is what drives me.

00:04:02.624 --> 00:04:04.200
You gotta live a sweet life.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.113
Right on, brother.

00:04:06.113 --> 00:04:08.661
First ascent, first time on the summit.

00:04:08.661 --> 00:04:10.828
Loving life!

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.150
(gentle instrumental music)

